<header><p class="st-kicker">city state · Anatolia and the Levant</p><h1 class="st-title">Kadesh</h1><p class="st-meta">1500 BCE – 1200 BCE (approx.) · capital Kadesh</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Kadesh, a fortified Syrian city on the Orontes that led resistance to Egypt and gave its name to the great chariot battle of 1274 BCE.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-kadesh">Kadesh</a>, at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tell-nebi-mend">Tell Nebi Mend</a> south of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/homs">Homs</a>, controlled the route through the Homs gap between the coast and inner <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/syrian-arab-republic">Syria</a>. In the 15th century BCE its king, backed by the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/mitanni-empire">Mitanni Empire</a>, led the Canaanite and Syrian coalition that <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thutmose-iii">Thutmose III</a> of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/egyptian-empire-new-kingdom">Egyptian Empire New Kingdom</a> defeated at <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/megiddo">Megiddo</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Its kings governed a compact territory of the upper <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/orontes-river">Orontes</a> and were courted by every great power. In the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/akhetaten">Amarna</a> age King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aitakkama">Aitakkama</a> went over to the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/hittite-empire">Hittite Empire</a> and raided Egyptian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vassal">vassals</a>, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hittite-empire">Hittites</a> kept <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-kadesh">Kadesh</a> as a vassal kingdom.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In 1274 BCE <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ramesses-ii">Ramesses II</a> fought <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muwatalli-ii">Muwatalli II</a> outside the city in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-kadesh">Battle of Kadesh</a>, after which the city stayed in Hittite hands. Kadesh was destroyed around 1200 BCE in the end of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/late-bronze-age">Late Bronze Age</a> and survived only as a village.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="city state, 1500 BCE – 1200 BCE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M24 82 V42 H32 V34 H40 V42 H46 V34 H54 V42 H60 V34 H68 V42 H76 V82 Z"/><path d="M44 82 V66 Q50 58 56 66 V82"/><path d="M34 54 H40 M60 54 H66"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">city state</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Anatolia and the Levant</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:29.85%;width:5.97%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1500 BCE – 1200 BCE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/16th-century-bce">16th century BCE</a> – <a href="/centuries/13th-century-bce">13th century BCE</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>city state</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Kadesh</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Aitakkama</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Syrian Semitic religion</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Akkadian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/syria">Syria</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Kinza, Qadesh</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=-1350&amp;focus=kadesh" aria-label="Kadesh on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5608 926 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Kadesh lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5928 1182L5996 1079M5928 1182L5863 1489M5928 1182L5852 1002"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5996 1079h0M5863 1489h0M5852 1002h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5928 1182h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5928 1182h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Kadesh. <a href="/atlas?year=-1350&amp;focus=kadesh">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

